' The body of plugin-host.puml / plugin-host-dark.puml. Not a diagram on its
' own: it carries no start marker, so PlantUML will not render this file
' directly.
'
' Careful: the start and end markers must not appear in this file at all, not
' even inside a comment. PlantUML scans for them lexically, so a comment naming
' one opens a second diagram here and the include fails with a line number
' pointing at neither file. See README.md.
'
' One message: the plugin host inside the plugins service, coloured by
' provenance - what already exists in Starling, what lifts from
' mumble-plugin-host unchanged in role, and what is written new for the port.
' Rationale, milestones and the context-method mapping live in
' ../PLUGIN-HOST-PLAN.md; this repeats none of it.
'
' The post-render passes in README.md are not optional for either half.

' A post-render step widens this single font name into a fallback stack, so a
' viewer without Inter gets a sans-serif rather than the monospace a missing
' font can fall back to.
skinparam defaultFontName Inter

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 44
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title The plugin host in Starling, coloured by provenance

header
The host runs in-process inside the plugins service; no C ABI survives the port.
The plugin-facing contract (MumblePlugin + PluginContext, ABI v3 / WASM v2) is unchanged, so built plugins load as-is.
endheader

actor "client" as client $c_faint
component "**gateway**\nreads the u16 type, parses nothing" as gw $c_faint

package "plugins service" as PS $c_pkg {
  component "**plane handler**  «ClientService»\ntype 26 relay - anti-spoof, caps\ntype 1010 Query · Opaque · Admin(refused)" as plane $c_have
  component "**PluginsRpc**  «gRPC»\nList · Enable · Install · Uninstall\nKvGet · KvScan · KvWrite" as rpc $c_have
  component "**Host**  «lifted»\nloader (abi_stable) · wasm (wasmtime)\ninstall (sha256) · registry · info envelope" as host $c_lift
  component "**plugins x N**  «lifted»\nnative cdylib or wasm component\neach owns its own tokio runtime" as plg $c_lift
  component "**StarlingContext**  «new»\nimplements PluginContext over\ngRPC + Roster + KV" as ctx $c_new
  component "**event fold**  «new»\nsession-view snapshot ->\nconnected · disconnected · registered" as ev $c_new
  component "**registry + plugin_kv**\npersisted enable state ·\nnamespaced plugin storage" as kv $c_have
}

component "**session-view**\nbroadcast snapshots" as sv $c_faint
component "**permissions · metadata · files**\nCheck · SetAcl · CreateRequest ·\nartifact by source_key" as svcs $c_faint
component "**operator-api**\n/v1/plugins  «new routes»" as op $c_faint

client -down-> gw : types 26 · 1010
gw -[$l_blue]-> plane : ClientEvent stream
op -[$l_blue]-> rpc : admin, HTTP -> gRPC
rpc --> host : enable · disable · install · uninstall
plane --> host : dispatch: 26 -> every plugin,\nOpaque -> one plugin by name
host --> plg : sync hooks, via spawn_blocking:\non_load · on_client_connected · on_plugin_message
plg --> ctx : PluginContext  «trait, unchanged»
ctx -[$l_blue]-> svcs : access checks · channel ops ·\nHandle::block_on per call
ctx --> kv : get_config · set_config · state
ctx --> plane : Fanout: Opaque / 26 out to sessions
sv -[$l_green]-> ev : snapshot stream
ev --> host : connected · disconnected ·\nregistered (user_id change)
host --> kv : registry rows · enable flags

note right of host $c_lift
  **What dies in the port.** The C ABI
  (ffi.rs), the C++ callback table
  (context.rs), the per-virtual-server
  host, and the wire admin messages
  146-151: Starling refuses in-band
  Admin by design, so administration
  is operator-api only.
end note

note right of ctx $c_new
  **The sync/async bridge.** Hooks are
  synchronous and plugins own their own
  runtimes, so the service invokes hooks
  on the blocking pool, never on a
  runtime worker, and context methods
  block_on a captured Handle. Precedent:
  userdata's Argon2 hashing.
end note

note bottom of ev $c_new
  **Eventually consistent, on purpose.**
  The C++ distributor fed plugins
  synchronously on the server thread.
  None of the four events can veto, so
  a snapshot-lagged greeter is harmless
  and the domain edge stays session-view.
end note

legend bottom
| «lifted», blue card | from mumble-plugin-host, role unchanged |
| «new», amber card | new code this plan adds |
| green card | already in Starling's plugins service today |
| grey card | a neighbour, already built |
| <color:$l_blue>blue edge</color> | gRPC |
| <color:$l_green>green edge</color> | broadcast, eventually consistent |
endlegend
